<title>HONG KONG: Wing On Holdings posts lower year profit.</title>
<headline>Wing On Holdings posts lower year profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   174.0	vs 344.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    60.0	 vs 55.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  29.44 gain vs 359.34 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    315.75     vs 625.06</p>
<p>    Turnover		     3,032.97   vs 2,827.5</p>
<p>    Company name		 Wing On International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 16-23</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 10</p>
<p>NOTE - Wing On International operates department stores and engages in insurance, property rental, hotel management, securities and commodities broking, and investment and financial services.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$13.34 million interest received on judgement debt, gain of HK$7.0 million on provision for bad and doubtful debts written back, gain of HK$17.5 million on legal costs recovered and loss of HK$8.4 million on legal costs incurred on litigation.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 87 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 27 cents) vs 115 cents (including interim dividend and special dividend).</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
